msgid "There are three main areas associated with the List:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3835
msgid "Taxonomies"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3837
msgid "Taxonomy Match Rule"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3838
msgid "See the section <strong>Document Taxonomies</strong> for the process to determine whether an individual External List term matches that on the Document."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3839
msgid "This flag indicates whether all the terms on the External List or at least one must match those on the Document for the External List to be considered matching the Document."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3841
msgid "This is a text area where optional comment or information can be made about the External List."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3843
msgid "This allows the External List to be paused from matching Documents."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3844
msgid "It is provided so that an External List can be withdrawn from processing temporarily without simply changing its status."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3846
msgid "The number of days after a Document was last modified that this List's log entries for it are kept. They are deleted once a day; empty or 0 keeps them. Only users who can delete Lists can change it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3847
msgid "List Notes"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3848
msgid "This is a text area where optional comment or information can be held about the External List."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3849
msgid "Use is made of the excerpt field as it intended to be a simple aide-memoire to administrators of the External Lists."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3851
msgid "This panel consists of two parts. First are the elements to create or edit an individual user record into the table of email addresses, followed by a searchable list of the email addresses associated with the list."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3852
msgid "Note that changes made to this User List are stored immediately. There is no separate process to update the data permanently or to cancel the edits made so far."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3853
msgid "This holds a list of individual users that will be sent an email when the External List is selected."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3854
msgid "Each user record will contain the user name and email address and an optional pause attribute that pauses the sending of emails to the user."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3855
msgid "This pause attribute allows the user details to be retained in the User List but notification emails will not be sent to the specific user."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3856
msgid "Document Taxonomies"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3857
msgid "These taxonomies are generally shown on the right part of the screen. They are the taxonomies that can be applied to Documents."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3858
msgid "At least one taxonomy term is required to be entered, although several can be."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3859
msgid "If there are multiple terms on the External List then the matching rule will used to determine whether just one term is needed for the External List to be selected or all terms present must match for notification."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3860
msgid "For hierarchical taxonomies, a term on the External List is considered matched if the term on the Document is either the same as that on the External List or is a child of the External List term."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3861
msgid "Because of this, it is not permitted to publish an External List when the terms entered contains a term and its parent since the term matching process means that the child term would be redundant."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3862
msgid "A Document can have additional terms present, i.e. it is not necessary that all Document terms must match."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3863
msgid "Publish"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3864
msgid "By default, Documents are only accessible to logged in users. Documents can be published, thus making them accessible to the world, by toggling their visibility in the \"Publish\" box in the top right corner. Any document marked as published will be accessible to anyone with the proper URL."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3865
msgid "Similarly these user lists need to be published for the list to be eligible to be selected for sending emails to its users."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3866
msgid "Permissions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3867
msgid "It is expected that the emailing administration process will be centralised with only a handful of External Lists being created. Therefore the full WordPress set of access permissions is not required."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3868
msgid "The permission <strong>edit_doc_ext_lists</strong> is supplied that allows users to create, update, and publish any External List."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3869
msgid "The permission <strong>delete_doc_ext_lists</strong> is supplied that allows users to delete any External List."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3870
msgid "The permission <strong>read_doc_ext_lists</strong> is supplied that allows users to see the External Lists, the email logs and the External List part of the Document screen, and to send External List emails for Documents they can edit."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3873
msgid "Document External Lists"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3874
msgid "Below is a list of all Document External Lists used to send email notifications to external users on an update to a Document. Click the list title to edit the document list."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3875
msgid "To add a new Document External List, click <strong>Add Document External List</strong> at the top of the screen."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3876
msgid "Note that whilst this functionality is primarily intended for people that are not users of this site, any email address can be used."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3880
msgid "Notification emails can be sent (or re-sent) for published Documents by clicking on the button \"Send notification emails\" (to internal users) or \"Send external emails\" (to  external users)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3881
msgid "Internal users are those with user-ids on the site. They can decide whether they wish to receive these notifications or not and whether a copy of the document should be attached the mail."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3882
msgid "This data can also be updated by Administrators (also using Bulk Editing functions)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3883
msgid "External users normally do not have a sign-on. Notifications are based on the concept of External Lists. A list will contain one or more taxonomy terms that will be matched again the document terms."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3884
msgid "Every published External List (except those marked as Paused) will be tested to see whether its terms match those on the Document."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3885
msgid "Those that match are listed below the button (only for users with the read_doc_ext_lists permission). If the user can maintain the External List, then they can choose to not send the mail to a List by unchecking the List before sending the Notification."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3886
msgid "A term on the List matches with one on the Document if they are same or, for hierarchical taxonomies, the List term is a parent of the Document term."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3887
msgid "When there are several terms on the List, a rule can be set so that the List is matched if either any term matches or all terms on the List must match."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3888
msgid "Potentially several Lists may match the Document. Emails will be sent to every user (except those individually paused) on each list that is matched."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3889
msgid "Document Email Extra Text"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3890
msgid "You can include some message-specific additional text with the notification emails."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3892
msgid "The template used (Internal or External) has to contain the tag \"%extra%\" in it to use this capability."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3893
msgid "If neither template contains the tag then the various options are not shown."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3894
msgid "A checkbox which is initially disabled with label \"Add Extra Text\" is placed next to each Send button."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3895
msgid "On entering some text in the text field, the checkboxes will become active if the template allows it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3896
msgid "The extra text will only be included if the corresponding checkbox is checked when the send button is clicked."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpdr-email-notice.php:3897
msgid "The Extra text can contains html tags to better format the output."
msgstr ""

